  "title": "# Blueprints switch notes, tasks and to-dos too (Brett, Nov 7) Depends on build `plan-blueprints` (…",
  "asked": "# Blueprints switch notes, tasks and to-dos too (Brett, Nov 7) Depends on build `plan-blueprints` (blueprint@1, Plan Studio Blueprints, context submenu). If it hasn't landed yet, base on branch claude/plan-blueprints (fetch it) and coordinate; don't duplicate its contract. 1. Switching the active blueprint switches EVERYTHING scoped to it: Plan Studio plans, AND AmberX/console notes, tasks, to-do items and lists (notes-tasks plugin, amberx.items, amberx.lists). 2. Items/lists get an optional `blueprint` field (backward compatible). Existing notes/tasks/to-dos go to the same blueprint the existing plans went to. 3. Global lists: some lists are shared across all blueprints. \"Quick notes\" is global by default. A per-list switch \"show in every blueprint\". 4. Voice: \"add X to quick notes\" always works; \"switch blueprint to X\" switches all of it. control@1, MCP, CLI. 5. Active blueprint visible in AmberX and the console (chip), settings in place, assets only, no hard-coded styling. UI Review three options (--choices). 6. Tests: switch filters plans + notes + tasks + to-dos; global lists stay; nothing lost. Add to Shipped features. Progress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push. ## Addendum (Brett, Nov 7): permanent Global group - Notes/tasks/to-do manager AND Plan Studio each get a permanent group called **Global** (can't be deleted or moved). - Global holds repo-wide items: they show no matter which blueprint is open. - Any plan, note, task, to-do or list can be set to Global (toggle + drag in), and back. - Quick notes lives in Global by default. Replaces the per-list \"show in every blueprint\" switch: Global is that switch. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
